[h1]Renault Trafic I T800 — 1985[/h1]

A first-generation Renault Trafic for [b]Project Zomboid Build 42.21[/b]: short wheelbase, low roof and a panel cargo body without rear side windows. A modest work van to haul your supplies through Kentucky.

[h2]My first vehicle experiment[/h2]

This is [b]my first attempt at making a vehicle for Project Zomboid[/b], while trying to control Blender through a coding agent. The vehicle was generated from [b]official vehicle blueprints[/b], without using any existing 3D model. The body, interior, wheels and animations were built for this project.

It is an experiment that I intend to keep improving. Feedback on its appearance, handling and everyday use is welcome.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Original model of the 1985 Renault Trafic I T800 panel van.
[*]Two front seats and a cargo capacity of 120.
[*]Animated front doors, right sliding cargo door, twin rear doors and hood.
[*]The same cargo storage is accessible through the rear doors or the open sliding door.
[*]Clean bodywork in white or blue: approximately 70% white and 30% blue when vehicles are created.
[*]Modelled interior, textured wheels and transparent windscreen and front door glass.
[*]Natural vehicle spawns in parking, delivery and trades zones, as well as junkyards.
[*]Vanilla vehicle mechanics and loot. No other mod is required.
[/list]

[h2]Build and feedback[/h2]

Made for [b]Build 42.21[/b]. This first release is a work in progress. For bug reports, please include your game version, active mods and the circumstances of the issue. A written description is useful even without a screenshot.

[h2]Support the project[/h2]

